{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2565,2625p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj && sed -n '325,370p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '680,700p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '1,77p' deps.edn\"","aggregated_output":"   (let [walker (run-library forms opts :walker 1000000)\n         semantic (run-library forms opts :semantic 1000000)]\n     (is (= walker semantic) (str \"library lanes agree: \" (pr-str forms)))\n     walker))\n  ([forms opts lane step-limit]\n   (run-guest-ast (yang/compile-program (into (yang/library-for forms) forms) true opts)\n                  library-modules lane step-limit)))\n\n\n(defn- lib\n  \"The value of the single expression `form`, or the raw error outcome.\"\n  [form]\n  (let [[tag payload] (run-library [form])]\n    (if (= :yin.k/ok tag) payload [tag payload])))\n\n\n(deftest finally-unwinds-and-orders-cleanup\n  (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n    (doseq [[forms expected]\n            [['[(let [log (cell/new [])]\n                  (try (try (throw :body)\n                            (finally (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) :finally))))\n                       (catch Exception e (cell/get log))))]\n              [:yin.k/ok [:finally]]]\n             ['[(let [log (cell/new [])]\n                  (try (try (throw :body)\n                            (catch Exception e (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) :catch)))\n                            (finally (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) :finally))))\n                       (finally (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) :outer))))\n                  (cell/get log))]\n              [:yin.k/ok [:catch :finally :outer]]]\n             ['[(try (try (throw :body) (finally (throw :cleanup)))\n                     (catch Exception e e))]\n              [:yin.k/ok :cleanup]]]]\n      (is (= expected (run-library forms library-opts lane 1000000))\n          (str lane \" \" forms)))))\n\n\n(defn- run-cell-program\n  \"The value of running the compiled `program` (quoted forms) with `node`\n   spliced into the marker operand, on one lane — every call keeps its\n   call-site routing — or the thrown refusal's ex-data.\"\n  [program node lane]\n  (let [ast (walk/postwalk\n              (fn [n] (if (= n (u/v 'marker-operand)) node n))\n              (yang/compile-program\n                (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n                true\n                library-opts))]\n    (try\n      (run-guest-ast ast library-modules lane 1000000)\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n        [:thrown (select-keys (ex-data e) [:reason :effect])]))))\n\n\n(defn- run-cell-probe\n  \"The value of running the compiled probe program — `(probe <node>)`, so\n   the spliced `node` sits at a call's callee position — on one lane, or\n   the thrown refusal's ex-data.\"\n  [node lane]\n  (run-cell-program\n  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n  name on all four VMs. Plain Clojure in the test JVM takes the same path\n  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n  REPL.\n\n```sh\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\nThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\nnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\nDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\nwith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\nexits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\neach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\nscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\nunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\ndifferent namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\npackage:test names are ns-qualified (`dao.foo-test/bar-test`).\n\n`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\ncompile does not prune it when a source file is deleted or renamed. The\naggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\nstale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\nbefore relying on that to prove a deletion or rename took effect.\n\n### Ledger commit hygiene: never commit a conflict marker\n\nThe append-only ledgers (`docs/agents/known-gaps.md`,\n`orchestrator-logs/*.md`, `docs/agents/routing-status.md`) resolve rebase\nand merge conflicts by the union rule, which means conflicts are common —\nand a conflict marker that reaches a commit silently corrupts the record\n(measured: the 2026-10-30 rebase landed a log with three committed\n`<<<<<<<`/`>>>>>>>` markers and dropped records the union was supposed to\nkeep; caught by the architect four rounds later). Before committing ANY\nchange to a ledger file:\n\n```sh\ngit diff --cached | grep -E '^\\+(<{7}|={7}$|>{7})' && echo CONFLICT-MARKERS-STAGED\ngit grep -E '^(<{7}|={7}$|>{7})' -- docs/agents/known-gaps.md orchestrator-logs docs/agents/routing-status.md\n```\n\nIf either hits, the commit stops until the union is redone. When resolving\na ledger conflict, prefer regenerating the union from both sides' section\nlists over hand-merging, and re-read the result against BOTH parents before\nstaging.\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\" \"build/antlr/php/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
