he host\n   value it publishes; profiles maps each export symbol to its UCF 7.5.2\n   profile record in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`. Every\n   binding must carry a profile, and the profile's class must be `:pure`,\n   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\n   `:yin.k/host-state` `:none`. An `:effectful` export returns an\n   effect minted by `make-effect` for the engine to interpret and\n   performs no IO itself; `stream/make` is exactly such a constructor.\n   Each export's declared effect set is also entered in the registry's\n   identity-keyed `:callable-effects`, which the engine checks an\n   effect's kind against (D4).\n\n   The module is entered as an already-linked manifest with\n   `:yin.module/tree` absent, `:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its\n   exports listed under `:yin.module/primitives` by profile address; the\n   exports themselves are its `:slice`, and its `:address` and\n   `:derivation` are nil because no content was fetched or derived: the\n   host is the boundary.\"\n  [registry module-name fns profiles]\n  (doseq [sym (sort-by str (keys fns))]\n    (check-binding! module-name sym (get profiles sym)))\n  (-> (or registry (empty-registry))\n      (update :callable-effects\n              (partial merge-with into)\n              (vm/callable-effects fns profiles))\n      (assoc-in (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n                {:manifest {:yin.module/name module-name,\n                            :yin.module/derivations {},\n                            :yin.module/primitives\n                            (into {} (map (fn [[sym _f]]\n                                            [sym (:yin.k/profile\n                                                   (get profiles sym))]))\n                                  fns)},\n                 :address nil,\n                 :derivation nil,\n                 :slice fns,\n                 :stores {}})))\n\n\n(defn host-export-profile\n                   nil\n                   (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e (ex-message e)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Slice 7: the guest collection and higher-order library\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private library-modules\n  \"The library's whole host surface: the `kind` module, the `portable`\n   adapters of the data exports the collection predicates read, and the\n   `cell` module. Every outcome-model program's emitted call routing reads\n   `cell/authentic?` once a callee passes the cell-ref shape pre-filter,\n   and a spliced `cell/new` mints genuine references (the engine seals\n   them under the test composition's capability secret), so the lane's\n   registry supplies the cell host as the linked compositions' do.\"\n  (let [host (fn [registry module-name fns arities]\n               (module/register-host-module\n                 registry module-name fns\n                 (into {} (map (fn [[op _]]\n                                 [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n                       fns)))\n        portable (into {}\n                       (map (fn [[source _]]\n                              (let [op (symbol (name source))]\n                                [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n                                                          (get data/data-module op))])))\n                       yang/library-adapters)]\n    (-> av-modules\n        (module/register-cell-module)\n        (host 'kind yang/kind-module yang/kind-arities)\n        (host 'portable portable\n              (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n                    (keys portable))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library-opts\n  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n   :adapters yang/library-adapters\n   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n  ;; so only the semantic lane can serve as the flag-sensitive control.\n  (testing \"negative control: without :tail? on the self-application depth grows\"\n    (let [run (fn [n] (semantic-run (strip-self-tail (countdown-ast :loop n :tail))))\n          [_ d0] (run 0)\n          [_ d100] (run 100)]\n      (is (> d100 (+ d0 50)) \"the semantic gate detects the missing flag\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Slice 5: the outcome model\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private effect-log (atom []))\n\n\n(def ^:private outcome-modules\n  (let [host (fn [name entries]\n               (fn [registry]\n                 (module/register-host-module\n                   registry name\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op f _]] [op f])) entries)\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op _ p]] [op p])) entries))))]\n    (-> av-modules\n        ((host 'portable\n               [['nth\n                 (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message (get data/data-module 'nth))\n                 (get data/data-profiles 'nth)]]))\n        ((host 'probe\n               [['note\n                 (fn [x] (swap! effect-log conj x) x)\n                 (vm/primitive-profile 'note :pure [1] #{} :none)]])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private outcome-opts\n  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n   :native (set (keys vm/primitives))\n   :adapters {'data/nth 'portable/nth}})\n\n\n(defn- outcome-ast\n  [forms]\n  (yang/compile-program forms true outcome-opts))\n\n196:   `:effectful` with a declared non-empty effect set, and no declared\n210:      :effectful (if (seq (:yin.k/effects profile))\n235:   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\n236:   `:yin.k/host-state` `:none`. An `:effectful` export returns an\n356:   is an `:effectful` pure effect constructor: it returns an effect\n359:  {'make (vm/primitive-profile 'make :effectful [0 1] #{:stream/make}\n361:   'put! (vm/primitive-profile 